{
  "an8.1:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 8.1 ",
  "an8.1:0.2": "1. Love ",
  "an8.1:0.3": "The Benefits of Love ",
  "an8.1:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "an8.1:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "an8.1:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "an8.1:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "an8.1:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "an8.1:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "an8.1:2.1": "“Mendicants, you can expect eight benefits when the heart’s release by love has been cultivated, developed, and practiced, made a vehicle and a basis, kept up, consolidated, and properly implemented. ",
  "an8.1:2.2": "What eight? ",
  "an8.1:2.3": "You sleep at ease. You wake happily. You don’t have bad dreams. Humans love you. Non-humans love you. Deities protect you. You can’t be harmed by fire, poison, or blade. If you don’t penetrate any higher, you’ll be reborn in a realm of divinity. ",
  "an8.1:2.4": "You can expect these eight benefits when the heart’s release by love has been cultivated, developed, and practiced, made a vehicle and a basis, kept up, consolidated, and properly implemented. ",
  "an8.1:3.1": "A mindful one who develops ",
  "an8.1:3.2": "limitless love ",
  "an8.1:3.3": "weakens the fetters, ",
  "an8.1:3.4": "seeing the ending of attachments. ",
  "an8.1:4.1": "Loving just one creature with a hateless heart ",
  "an8.1:4.2": "makes you a true person. ",
  "an8.1:4.3": "Sympathetic for all creatures, 